    "seconds": 47,
    "summary": "The application is healthy again. The cause was a feature flag, not the cart pod itself.\n\n**What I found**\n- The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `cartFailure` set to `defaultVariant: \"on\"`. The upstream demo ships this flag as `off`. The flag's other fields match upstream, so the default is the only thing that changed.\n- The ConfigMap was modified at <time> by a field manager named `OpenAPI-Generator`. The `cart` and `flagd` deployments were restarted at the same moment.\n- The earlier frontend `ECONNREFUSED` errors at 16:18 came from the cart service being down before the restart. They are not the current state.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Set `cartFailure.defaultVariant` to `off` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. Nothing else in the file was changed.\n- Restarted the `flagd` deployment so its init container copies the corrected file. The new pod's init log shows `\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"`.\n\n**Current state**\n- All 24 deployments are at 1/1 or 2/2 Ready, with no restarts since the rollout.\n- The `cart` logs show no errors since the fix.\n\n**Not verified**\n- Helm isn't installed here, so I couldn't diff against the rendered manifest. The upstream default is my basis for `off`.\n- The `OpenAPI-Generator` writer is still unexplained. If something re-applies the bad value, or a `helm upgrade` resets it, the problem will come back. Whoever owns that process should find out what changed the flag.",
    "timed_out": false,
